          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Graphene is one of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid"} solid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+of+matter"} phases
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/carbon"} carbon
          %p#PrimeExampleOfTopologicalPhase
            Graphene is a prime example (and among the first to be discovered) of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phase+of+matter"} topological phase of matter
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                at coarse resolution (currently accessible to
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-reversal+symmetry"} time-reversal
                and space inversion-symmetric)
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+semi-metal"} topological semi-metal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+band"} valence band
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conduction+band"} conduction band
                which closes only over two
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+points"} Dirac points
                in its
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brillouin+torus"} Brillouin torus
            %li
              %p
                at finer resolution – namely when the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin-orbit+coupling"} spin-orbit coupling
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"} electrons
                is resolved (thought to be
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∼
                      %msup
                        %mn 10
