                %a{:href => "#MHSSKM06"} MHSSKM06
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
                and hence too small for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experimental
                observation, currently), which reveals a small energy gap opening at the two would-be Dirac points – graphene appears as a (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time-reversal+symmetry"}> time-reversal symmetric
                )
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulator"} topological insulator
                (
                %a{:href => "#KaneMele05a"}> Kane &amp; Mele 05a
                ), whose non-trivial
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phase+of+matter"} topological phase
                is witnessed by the non-trivial
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kane-Mele+invariant"} Kane-Mele invariant
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group+of+order+two"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
